    thinking: "**Defining Types Now**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the types in `src/types.ts`. I\'ve begun to define `CityRegion` as a union type. I\'m also examining the structure for the `MenuItem` interface. I will be looking to ensure that the code is well-structured and typed.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the `FoodSpot` interface, adding comprehensive details like dietary tags and payment types. I am adding fields like `topDeal` and `menu` to provide comprehensive information about the food spots. I am also defining `RadiusFilter` and `PriceFilter` to support filtering. I am looking to cover all the bases to ensure the data is complete and usable.\n\n\n**Defining Filter Options**\n\nI\'m working on the data for `foodSpots.ts` now, specifically the filter options. I\'m expanding the `PriceRange` type with new values such as \'under50\', \'under100\', and \'under150\'. Also, I am going to define `ViewMode` as a type with possible values of \'deck\', \'grid\', and \'radar\'. I\'m aiming to create a dynamic and user-friendly experience when looking at food spots. Now I need to define the food spots in Mumbai and Tamil Nadu.\n\n\n**Populating Restaurant Data**\n\nNow I\'m diving into adding actual restaurant data, starting with Mumbai. I\'m focusing on populating the `foodSpots.ts` file with entries for places like Kyani & Co., Kalyan Bhelpuri, and Tibbs Frankie. I\'m paying close attention to categorizing them, noting their top deals, and creating their menu items, including prices and any pro tips provided. I\'m focusing on ensuring data integrity and consistency.\n\n\n**Adding Restaurant Data**\n\nI\'m now building out more restaurant data. I\'m focusing on Chennai and Madurai, looking at Murugan Idli, Ratna Cafe, and the Jigarthanda shop. I am taking note of their special deals, categorizing them appropriately, and recording their menu items and associated pro tips. I\'m focusing on detailed menu data for each place, including prices and the \"pro tips\".\n\n\n\n"
